<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
        REBRAND FOLLOW-UP for 038 — repoint the character-forge remote_entry_url from
        the sibling UI's OLD k8s Service short-name (snapdragon-character-forge-ui) to
        its rebranded one (hugmesh-character-forge-ui).

        WHY A NEW CHANGESET INSTEAD OF EDITING 038 IN PLACE.
        038-register-character-forge-module.xml is MERGED (#86) and may already have run
        in live databases, so it is immutable history:
          1. remote_entry_url lives INSIDE 038's <changeSet>, so rewriting it changes the
             changeSet's Liquibase MD5. Every DB that already ran 038 would then fail
             startup with ValidationFailedException on a checksum mismatch.
          2. Even ignoring checksums, an in-place edit would NOT actually fix an already
             migrated DB: 038 is recorded RAN and never re-executes, so the live row
             would keep pointing at the dead snapdragon-* Service forever. Only a NEW
             changeset can migrate an existing row.
        The one in-place precedent in this repo (PR #83's "Snapdragon — Federation Host"
        -> "HugMesh — Federation Host" display_name edit in 010) was an explicitly-flagged
        cosmetic exception. That same PR #83 deliberately LEFT every
        http://snapdragon-<slug>[-ui]:8080/remoteEntry.json seed value alone, on the
        stated grounds that they are "live routing targets owned by those sibling repos'
        own (separate) rebrand, not cosmetic text". This changeset IS that separate
        rebrand arriving for character-forge, so it migrates the value rather than
        retro-editing the shipped INSERT.

        DEPLOY ORDERING. The value here must match the sibling's actual k8s Service name.
        The Service/Deployment/HTTPRoute for the Character Forge UI are renamed
        snapdragon-character-forge-ui -> hugmesh-character-forge-ui in the generator's
        specs/cluster/manifests/character-forge/ manifests as part of the SAME
        character-forge rebrand wave. This changeset must not reach a cluster before
        that manifest rename does, or the remote entry would resolve to a Service that
        does not exist yet. (The row is registered enabled=false / visibility='internal'
        by 038, so an in-flight window is inert rather than user-visible.)

        NOT RENAMED HERE (frozen, per reserved-prefixes.yaml rev 9 + the merged 038
        federation registration): the FEATURE SLUG 'character-forge' itself — the row's
        slug, metadata.mountAt '/character-forge', the fe-gateway /character-forge/**
        and BFF /bff/character-forge/** route prefixes. Only the BRAND PREFIX on the
        sibling service's hostname changes.

        SAFETY. The preCondition matches the row ONLY while it still carries the exact
        pre-rebrand URL, so the changeset is idempotent (re-runs MARK_RAN) and it never
        clobbers an operator/superadmin override of remote_entry_url (the admin control
        plane added in #85 can rewrite this column). The same predicate is repeated in
        the <where> clause so a concurrent override between the precondition check and
        the UPDATE is still a no-op rather than a silent overwrite. updated_at is bumped
        to mirror what ModuleRegistryService/AdminModuleService do on any row mutation.
        A rollback restores the pre-rebrand URL.
    -->

    <changeSet id="039-1-rebrand-character-forge-remote-entry" author="federation">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="1">
                SELECT COUNT(*) FROM federation_modules
                 WHERE slug = 'character-forge'
                   AND remote_entry_url = 'http://snapdragon-character-forge-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json'
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>

        <update tableName="federation_modules">
            <column name="remote_entry_url" value="http://hugmesh-character-forge-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json"/>
            <column name="updated_at" valueComputed="${now}"/>
            <where>
                slug = 'character-forge'
                AND remote_entry_url = 'http://snapdragon-character-forge-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json'
            </where>
        </update>

        <rollback>
            <update tableName="federation_modules">
                <column name="remote_entry_url" value="http://snapdragon-character-forge-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json"/>
                <column name="updated_at" valueComputed="${now}"/>
                <where>
                    slug = 'character-forge'
                    AND remote_entry_url = 'http://hugmesh-character-forge-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json'
                </where>
            </update>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
